{"name":"Top Banana","hex":"#fad873","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"top banana","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The boss, the leader.","The principal comedian in a vaudeville or burlesque show."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/top_banana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Top Banana (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Top Banana is a 1991 platform game published by Hex for the Acorn Archimedes, Amiga, Atari ST, and CDTV. The game is about trying to save the planet from environmental threats using love, and in line with the game's environmentalist theme, it was released with recycled cardboard packaging. Top Banana's music was produced by electronic music duo Coldcut, and the game features a techno music video as an introduction. Some reviewers praised Top Banana's techno soundtrack and original environmental plot, while others heavily criticized the game due to its repetitive and difficult gameplay and difficult to parse graphics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ce/Top_Banana%2C_Amiga_Title_Screen.png/330px-Top_Banana%2C_Amiga_Title_Screen.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_Banana_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q7824424"},{"title":"Top Banana (Arrested Development)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Top Banana\" is the second episode of the American television satirical sitcom Arrested Development. Written by series creator Mitchell Hurwitz and co-executive producer John Levenstein, and directed by producer Anthony Russo, it premiered on the Fox Network in the United States on November 9, 2003. The series, narrated by Ron Howard, follows the Bluths, a formerly wealthy, dysfunctional family, who made their money from property development. In the episode, the Bluths' banana stand is burned down, and Tobias, now wanting to become an actor, auditions for a commercial."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a6/Top_Banana.png/330px-Top_Banana.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_Banana_(Arrested_Development)","wikidata":"Q48465901"},{"title":"Banana","blocks":[{"text":"A banana is an elongated, edible fruit that is botanically a berry produced by several kinds of large treelike herbaceous flowering plants in the genus Musa. In some countries, cooking bananas are called plantains, distinguishing them from dessert bananas. The fruit is variable in size, color and firmness, but is usually elongated and curved, with soft flesh rich in starch covered with a peel, which may have a variety of colors when ripe. It grows upward in clusters near the top of the plant. Almost all modern edible seedless (parthenocarp) cultivated bananas come from two wild species – Musa acuminata and Musa balbisiana, or their hybrids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Bananavarieties.jpg/330px-Bananavarieties.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banana","wikidata":"Q503"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Anthony_Russo_%2848385343301%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Anthony_Russo_%2848385343301%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Anthony_Russo_%2848385343301%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Anthony_Russo_%2848385343301%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Anthony_Russo_%2848385343301%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Anthony_Russo_%2848385343301%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Anthony Russo directed the episode.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnthony_Russo_(48385343301)_(cropped).jpg"},{"